results.description:
There are currently no plans for a new conversation between Vladimir Putin and Donald Trump, according to Dmitry Peskov.

He added that such a conversation could be arranged quickly if both leaders desire it.

Key takeaways from the press secretary's briefing:

- Mediation in a complex process like the resolution of the situation in Ukraine is conducted discreetly;

- Putin has not yet made a decision on the composition of the Russian negotiating group in the three-way talks on Ukraine;

- There are no plans to hold a meeting between Putin and the members of the Russian negotiating group in the three-way talks on Ukraine;

- "megaphone diplomacy" can only harm the resolution of the situation in Ukraine;

- A decision on Putin's participation in the G20 summit has not yet been made, and the invitation will be considered;

- The United States is doing a lot to resolve the situation, while Europe is doing a lot to provoke further military action;

- Russia has not heard a single statement from Europe that would indicate a desire to de-escalate and take Moscow's interests into account;

- Russia sees a positive development in the fact that some European countries are trying to understand Moscow's concerns, but the process does not go beyond that;

- Cooperation between Russia and China in the energy sector has untapped potential;

- Putin and Li Qiang did not discuss preparations for a deal on the "Sila Baykala" gas pipeline;

- Russia is guided solely by its own interests when making decisions regarding foreign assets.

⚡️Two Majors

